===Verb===
{{en-verb||++|forgot|past2=forgat|past2_qual=obsolete|forgotten|past_ptc2=forgot|past_ptc2_qual=archaic or colloquial}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lose]] [[remembrance]] of.
#: {{ux|en|I have '''forgotten''' most of the things I learned in school.}}
#* {{RQ:Nashe Christs Teares|folio=60|verso=1|passage=VVe (of all earthlings) are Gods vtmoſt ſubiects, the laſt (in a manner) that he bought to his obedience: ſhal we then '''forgette''' that vvee are any ſubiects of hys, becauſe (as amongſt his Angels) he is not viſibly conuerſant amongſt vs?}}
#* {{RQ:Williams Velveteen Rabbit|passage=For at least two hours the Boy loved him, and then Aunts and Uncles came to dinner, and there was a great rustling of tissue paper and unwrapping of parcels, and in the excitement of looking at all the new presents the Velveteen Rabbit was '''forgotten'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=Lawrence R. Bourne
|title=Well Tackled!
|chapter=4|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5387037W
|passage=Technical terms like ferrite, perlite, graphite, and hardenite were bandied to and fro, and when Paget glibly brought out such a rare exotic as ferro-molybdenum, Benson '''forgot''' that he was a master ship-builder,{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|author=Robert Dean Frisbee|title=The Book of Puka-Puka|publisher=Eland|year_published=2019|page=35
|passage=Everybody, old and young, laughs uproariously at this and immediately '''forgets''' all about it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Guy Beiner|title=Forgetful Remembrance|page=625
|passage=In conditions of unlimited global-digital 'web-memory' (labelled by one critic a 'globital age'), social remembering and '''forgetting''' have become functions of algorithm-based search technologies that mine data from users {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[unintentionally]] not [[do]], [[neglect]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''forgot''' to buy flowers for my wife at our 14th wedding anniversary.}}
#* {{RQ:Dunsany Pegana
|passage=Pray, thou, therefore, to Slid, and forget not Slid, and it may be that Slid will not '''forget''' to send thee Death when most thou needest it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[unintentionally]] leave something behind.
#: {{ux|en|I '''forgot''' my car keys in the living room.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[cease]] [[remembering]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's just '''forget''' about it.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''forgot''' having already visited this city.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|loosely|informal}} To not [[realize]] something (regardless of whether one has ever known it).
#: {{ux|en|People '''forget''' how much work goes into what we do.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} {{non-gloss|[[euphemism|Euphemism]] for}} [[fuck]], [[screw]] {{qualifier|a mild oath}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''Forget''' you!}}

====Usage notes====
* In sense 1 and 4 this is a [[catenative]] verb that takes the ''gerund (-ing)''.
* In sense 2 this is a [[catenative]] verb that takes the ''to'' infinitive.
* See [[Appendix:English catenative verbs]]

